codex
I found the precise infrastructure defect: Lean 4.22 resolves its executable through `/proc/<getpid>/exe`, but this audit sandbox exposes a different PID namespace (`getpid()` returned `3` while `/proc/3/exe` does not exist). I’m applying a narrow runtime shim that redirects only `/proc/<digits>/exe` lookups to `/proc/self/exe`; it does not alter Lean code, project files, theorem checking, or any other filesystem read. This should let the pinned binary identify itself normally.
apply patch
